WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.865 --> 00:00:02.720
I walk into the apartment,
I open the door,

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.690
and immediately a smell hits you.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.520
Now, I can't really describe this smell,

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.930
but it's very unpleasant.

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.560
So now, I begin to just do your
general just looking around.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:13.662
Then all of a sudden I'm like,

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:15.450
it looks like the wall is moving.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:20.040
So, hundreds and hundreds of
roaches on this guy's wall.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.390
That's just when you walk in.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:25.280
His mattress was completely
infested with roaches.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.190
You could barely see that the mattress,

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:29.310
the color of the mattress.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.700
I'll put it that way. It looked brown.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.400
My name is Larry Bernhardt.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.010
I work for Top Notch Pest Control.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.700
I've been an exterminator
for about 13 years now.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:40.690
Most pests will reproduce
according to food,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.560
and, unfortunately, New York
is severely overpopulated.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.730
So there's an abundance
of food and shelter

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.910
for them to just keep reproducing.

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:51.950
You know, ton of rats.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:52.783
[Interviewer] Right.

00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:55.210
Rodents, roaches, you name it,

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.030
it's pretty much in New York.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.380
A few places I would never want to live

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:03.780
is pretty much next to
old, multi-unit buildings.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.710
So like your prewar buildings.

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:07.100
That's basically any
building that was like

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.743
built before World War
II in New York City.

00:01:09.743 --> 00:01:11.442
There's a bunch of holes in the buildings.

00:01:11.442 --> 00:01:14.170
They're not up-to-date regulation-wise.

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:15.490
Old piping, stuff like that,

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:17.760
will always cause pest problems,

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.440
a bunch of places for the
rodents and pests to hide.

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:23.810
And, yes, next to a park
because you don't know

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.900
what's going on inside of the
park with all the rodents.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.030
Rats tend to burrow, and if
there's a bunch of ground

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:33.000
that they can burrow into,
they're gonna tend to nest there.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.380
Once they start looking for food,

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.630
if there's not food ready for them,

00:01:35.630 --> 00:01:37.370
they're gonna make their
way into buildings.

00:01:37.370 --> 00:01:39.680
Especially in the winter,
they're looking for warmth.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.450
If your building is the
closest to the park,

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:43.260
you're gonna be the
first place that they go.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.940
So the worst floor to live on

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.430
would actually be the
ground level or first floor.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.840
Pests generally start
to go from ground up,

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.020
especially rodents.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:54.050
So you'll get your rat
issues and your mouse issues

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:55.830
from the ground up.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.500
The pest problem is
terrible near restaurants.

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.910
It really has to do with the garbage,

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:03.450
them disposing of it in the proper ways

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.100
and also in, like, a timely manner.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.840
You know, a lot of these restaurants,

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.590
they'll just have like a
dumpster out in the back,

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.200
and they're just putting
the garbage right there.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.960
What happens is, after nighttime,

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.170
the rats are just going to eat.

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.800
So as they eat, they'll reproduce more.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.320
And also with these takeout restaurants,

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.150
if they are having a pest problem,

00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.400
and one actually has a roach egg in it,

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:24.250
and now you're putting
it into your cabinet,

00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:27.230
yes, you know have an
infestation of roaches.

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.230
I think most New Yorkers don't know that

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:34.420
a roach egg will typically
have 30 to 40 babies in it.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:37.110
So generally somebody sees one roach,

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.670
they kill it, and they
kind of move on with life.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:41.860
They don't realize that the
first thing you should be doing

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.530
is calling a professional or at least

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:46.330
trying to take care of it on your own,

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.623
that there's probably 30 more
that you're just not seeing.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.680
The most important
things would actually be

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.300
taking the trash out every night

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.380
and making sure there's no
dirty dishes in the sink.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.940
Also, no clutter.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.440
Clutter is the worst because
once something gets in,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:03.530
you're not gonna be able to find it

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:05.670
due to all the clutter
and the messy conditions.

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:07.380
You know, we're never gonna be ahead of it

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:12.380
until people start taking
sanitary matters very seriously.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.450
I make my way into the bedroom,

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.120
his mattress was completely
infested with roaches.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.460
I've never seen that in all the years

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:22.970
I've been doing pest control.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:23.803
[Interviewer] What does that mean,

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:24.636
infested with roaches?

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:29.490
You could barely see that the mattress,

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:30.640
the color of the mattress.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.951
I'll put it that way. It looked brown.

